# FerryCast crontab — the recommended deployment.
#
#   crontab -e   and paste, adjusting paths.
#
# Phase 1 of the PRD is just the capture line: ship that first and data accrues while
# everything else is built.

FERRYCAST_CONFIG=/srv/ferrycast/config/ferrycast.toml
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
PATH=/srv/ferrycast/.venv/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SHORT VERSION. One line runs every collector at its own cadence — capture (with the
# geometric read inside it), deck space, the vessel tracker, both forecasts, backgrounds,
# aggregation and retention. Due-ness lives in the `job_runs` table, so a tick that fires
# late or twice does not double-run anything, and this is the only way to poll the vessel
# tracker from cron: it is the one collector with no command of its own.
#
# */5 * * * *   ferrycast schedule --once >> /var/log/ferrycast/ferrycast.log 2>&1
#
# Everything below is the same pipeline spelled out job by job, for a deployment that wants
# separate logs and separate failure domains. Use one or the other, not both.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# R1 + R2 — archive a frame from each camera and scrape deck space and the departures board.
# Neither costs money. Capture is here because it is the one irreversible step: reading can
# always be done later, but a frame not taken at 14:15 is gone for good. Five minutes is a
# courtesy rate, not a technical floor — the camera publishes a new JPEG every minute, so
# this takes one frame in five of what it already generates. Do not go faster.
*/5 * * * *   ferrycast capture >> /var/log/ferrycast/capture.log 2>&1; ferrycast scrape >> /var/log/ferrycast/scrape.log 2>&1

# Read the frames just captured, geometrically. No API call — about 19ms a frame — so this
# runs on every cycle rather than being deferred like the paid path. It also catches up on a
# backlog a few frames at a time, which is what fills in a terminal calibrated after
# collection started. Under `ferrycast run` this happens inside the capture job; on cron it
# needs its own line.
*/5 * * * *   ferrycast lanes >> /var/log/ferrycast/lanes.log 2>&1

# The per-hour empty-compound references the line above differences against. Daily, because
# it only has to keep pace with the sun: a two-week trailing median moves about four degrees
# of solar declination in a day.
11 3 * * *    ferrycast backgrounds >> /var/log/ferrycast/backgrounds.log 2>&1

# The ECCC forecasts — the water this route crosses, and the compound you wait in. Both are
# reissued a few times a day and amended between, and there is no "latest" path to ask for,
# so each run walks back through hours until it finds one. Drop these two lines if you have
# configured neither.
7 */3 * * *   ferrycast marine >> /var/log/ferrycast/weather.log 2>&1; ferrycast shore >> /var/log/ferrycast/weather.log 2>&1

# R4 — turn yesterday's readings into one record per sailing. Free: this runs on deck
# space and lane geometry, so every sailing gets a record whether or not any frame was ever
# read by the model.
23 3 * * *    ferrycast aggregate --date yesterday >> /var/log/ferrycast/aggregate.log 2>&1

# Retention plus the weekly digest. Frames aged past `thin_unextracted_after_days` and still
# unread are thinned down to the ones an extraction would actually use, so the archive stays
# bounded (roughly 2.8 GB/year rather than 5.7) without losing the ability to analyse any
# sailing. `health --strict` exits non-zero when something is wrong, so cron's MAILTO only
# reaches you when there is a problem to read about.
41 4 * * 0    ferrycast prune >> /var/log/ferrycast/prune.log 2>&1
47 4 * * 0    ferrycast health --window 7 --strict

# NOTHING ABOVE SPENDS MONEY. The vision model runs only when you ask:
#     ferrycast check --origin ERL --time 15:25          # ~$0.004, reads the camera now
#     ferrycast extract --essential --for-date 2026-07-04  # ~$0.09, analyse one past day
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: have the model read every day automatically (~$2.65/month).
#
# Geometry already reads any calibrated terminal for nothing, so this buys two things it
# cannot give: a reading at a terminal with no calibration, and a judgement on the awkward
# frames — fog, glare, snow, roadworks — where a model looking at the scene is worth paying
# for. Uncomment to build that record continuously:
#
# 17 2 * * *   ferrycast extract --essential --for-date yesterday >> /var/log/ferrycast/extract.log 2>&1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# After changing the prompt (bump `prompt_version` in the config), re-extract the backlog
# by hand rather than on a schedule:
#   ferrycast extract --limit 500 && ferrycast aggregate --all
